score_pct: 48.6
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. TEA mentions
    'malformed TOML rejected' but no test specifically distinguishes NotFound from
    parse/permission errors. Reviewer did not flag this pattern.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified: 'CWE-209 protection: CliError::ServerError Display\
    \ does not expose the inner String \u2014 error.rs:6-7'. TEA also wrote CWE-209\
    \ tests. Dev implemented safe Display impls. However, the stderr eprintln leaking\
    \ was not flagged \u2014 the Display impl is safe but the printing path was not\
    \ scrutinized. Partial catch at best."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests for CRLF in tenant_id, and Dev implemented
    CRLF stripping in with_tenant(). However, the actual finding is that tenant_id
    is a raw String instead of using axiathon-core's validated TenantId type. Reviewer
    even flagged the inconsistent sanitization but did not flag the missing TenantId
    newtype usage. The type-safety gap was not caught.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as HIGH: 'Workspace dependency hygiene violation \u2014\
    \ None of these were added to workspace dependencies. The crate uses direct version\
    \ specs (clap_complete = \"4\", comfy-table = \"7\", etc.). This violates the\
    \ workspace-level dependency declaration rule.'"
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as MEDIUM: 'ClientConfig silently ignores unknown TOML\
    \ fields (no deny_unknown_fields) \u2014 An operator who adds token = \"secret\"\
    \ to their config file gets no error, no warning. Should use #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]\
    \ to fail loudly.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as LOW: 'siem_client_rejects_newlines_in_token test\
    \ is vacuous \u2014 The assertion !client.has_auth_token() || { true } always\
    \ passes when has_auth_token() is true, because || { true } short-circuits to\
    \ true.'"
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    'let _ = config'. The reviewer found a different vacuous test (I5) but did not
    identify this separate zero-assertion issue.
